*venv*
*.sqlite3
.idea/
*.pyc
.env
*.log

build/
dist/

*.DS_Store
.vscode/

.coverage

# Dependencies
node_modules
.pnp
.pnp.js
.pnpm-store/

# Testing
coverage

# Turbo
.turbo

# The API's own log store (LOGS_DIR). `*.log` above catches `api.log`; the trace channel writes
# `.jsonl`, which it does not, so a local `pnpm dev` left `logs/traces/*.jsonl` staged and three
# commits carried one before anybody noticed. Runtime output either way, and re-created on boot.
apps/api/logs/

# Debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Misc
*.pem

.contractkit/
.local-storage/
# Locally cached artwork (ART_DIR). Fetched from the upstream the catalog points at, and
# re-fetchable, so it is a cache rather than anything to commit.
media/
.tanstack/tmp/

# Docker volume data (bind-mounted host paths)
.docvol/

# Operator-installed plugins (PLUGINS_DIR). Theirs, not the repo's — and in a dev
# checkout it is where you symlink a plugin you are working on, which is a local
# arrangement rather than something to commit.
apps/api/data/plugins/

# The rights-cleared music bed is the operator's own library, mounted at /music.
# The directory has to exist for the bind mount; its contents are never committed.
stream/music/*
!stream/music/.gitkeep
# The analysis sidecar is the first Python in the tree; these are its build droppings.
# The container installs from requirements.txt and never sees either.
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/

# Rendered by stream/crossfade.check.liq; regenerate rather than commit.
stream/*.check.wav
.tanstack/

# The Android listener is the second non-Node thing in the tree, and these are its build
# droppings. `build/` and `.idea/` above already cover most of it; the rest is Gradle's own
# caches and the SDK path, which names one machine's filesystem and is never committed.
.gradle/
.kotlin/
local.properties
*.iml
.cxx/
captures/
*.hprof

# The desktop app is the third non-Node thing in the tree, after the sidecar and the Android
# listener, and these are MSBuild's droppings. `bin/` and `obj/` are bare rather than anchored
# because nothing else in this repository uses either name, and a NuGet restore writes them beside
# every project rather than in one place.
bin/
obj/
.vs/
*.user
TestResults/
apps/desktop/artifacts/

# Signing keys, which live outside the repo and are ignored here anyway as a second line of
# defence. The upload key is the one artifact this project cannot regenerate: lose it and the
# published app can never be updated again, only replaced under a new application id.
*.jks
*.keystore

# Robert's own working notes, which name this install and this operator rather than the project.
# The `.local.md` suffix is the convention for exactly that and this file was tracked against it.
CLAUDE.local.md

# A per-developer Vite override: `VITE_ALLOWED_HOSTS` names whatever hostname a tunnel forwards
# through, which is one machine's arrangement rather than the project's.
.env.local
